# Supabase — shared instance, isolated schema
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co # Supabase project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key # Supabase anon/public key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key # Server-only service role key
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SCHEMA=agentdesk # Postgres schema name for this app (shared-schema mode, used by both browser + server Supabase clients)

# FRED (Federal Reserve Economic Data) — free, no credit card
# SERVER-ONLY. Used by /api/mortgage-rate and the Market Stats server component (MORTGAGE30US + MORTGAGE15US).
# Do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would inline the key into the browser bundle and allow quota abuse.
# Get a key at https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
FRED_API_KEY=your-fred-api-key # Server-only FRED API key for live mortgage rate data

# RapidAPI — Zillow Live Data Scraper
# SERVER-ONLY secret. Do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would inline it into the browser bundle.
# Consumed by lib/zillow.ts and /api/property-lookup.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP — required for the Property Comparator to work
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Create a free RapidAPI account at https://rapidapi.com/
#   2. Subscribe to the "Zillow.com Live Data Scraper" API host:
#      https://rapidapi.com/api-vortex-api-vortex-default/api/zillow-com-live-data-scraper-api
#      The host header used in lib/zillow.ts is:
#        zillow-com-live-data-scraper-api.p.rapidapi.com
#      Verify this matches the host shown on the RapidAPI listing you
#      subscribed to — if not, update ZILLOW_HOST in lib/zillow.ts.
#   3. Copy your X-RapidAPI-Key from the "Endpoints" tab and paste below.
#   4. Confirm your subscription tier has request quota remaining. A 403/429
#      from RapidAPI surfaces in the UI as "Data unavailable — check your
#      connection" and is almost always a quota/subscription issue, NOT a
#      network problem.
#   5. On Vercel, add RAPIDAPI_KEY in Project Settings → Environment Variables
#      and REDEPLOY. Env var changes do not apply to existing deployments.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TROUBLESHOOTING — "property not found" vs "connection error"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   • "No data found for this address" (yellow card)
#       RapidAPI returned 404. The address itself is the problem, not the
#       connection. Use the full USPS form:
#         123 Main St, Tampa, FL 33601
#       Always include city, 2-letter state, and ZIP. Verify on zillow.com
#       first — if Zillow can't find it, the API can't either.
#
#   • "Data unavailable — check your connection" (red card)
#       Network error, 401/403 (bad/missing key), 429 (rate limited), or 5xx
#       from RapidAPI. Diagnose in order:
#         a) Is RAPIDAPI_KEY set on the deployment? (Vercel env vars, then redeploy)
#         b) Are you subscribed to the exact host name above?
#         c) Is the monthly quota exhausted? (RapidAPI → My Apps → Usage)
#         d) Is the Zillow scraper host itself degraded? (check RapidAPI status)
#         e) Cold-start timeout: first request after idle can take 15–30s on
#            Vercel's free tier. Retry once.
#
#   • Test the key directly with curl to isolate app vs. RapidAPI:
#       curl -H "x-rapidapi-key: $RAPIDAPI_KEY" \
#            -H "x-rapidapi-host: zillow-com-live-data-scraper-api.p.rapidapi.com" \
#            "https://zillow-com-live-data-scraper-api.p.rapidapi.com/byaddress?address=1600%20Pennsylvania%20Ave%20NW%2C%20Washington%2C%20DC%2020500"
#     200 + JSON → key works; problem is per-address.
#     401/403  → key invalid, unsubscribed, or wrong host.
#     429      → rate limited.
#     5xx      → upstream Zillow/RapidAPI outage.
#
#   • Check Vercel function logs for the exact upstream status:
#       Vercel → Deployments → (your deployment) → Functions → /api/property-lookup
#     lib/zillow.ts logs the host, label, and HTTP status of every call.
RAPIDAPI_KEY=your-rapidapi-key # Server-only RapidAPI key for Zillow Live Data Scraper host
